-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 13 (repealed, ss 264-267), Chapter 14
-- (Offences affecting the public tranquility, public health, safety,
-- convenience, decency and morals, ss 267A-294) and Chapter 15 (Offences
-- relating to race, ss 295-298A).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt), quoted mechanically above each rule.
--
-- Part of the "justice-order" group; read the header of pc-justice-order.l4
-- first, which this module imports for its recital helper (`to wit`). The same
-- conventions hold: one facts record per family, flat BOOLEAN leaves, a
-- defining predicate per defining section, `offence under s N` and
-- `charge under s N` per punishing section.
--
-- Sections whose punishment turns on the RESULT of the act (ss 284, 285, 287,
-- 288, 289: "likely to cause hurt", "causes grievous hurt", "causes death")
-- are one offence each, and the charge builder picks the punishing paragraph
-- by the gravest result established (FORK JO-8).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-justice-order`

§ `Chapter 13 - (repealed)`

-- s 264. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

-- s 265. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

-- s 266. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

-- s 267. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

§ `Chapter 14 - Offences affecting the public tranquility, public health, safety, convenience, decency and morals`

§§ `s 267A - Affray`

-- 267A. Where 2 or more persons disturb the public peace by fighting in a public
-- place, they are said to "commit an affray".

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 267A, 267B - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Affray Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `2 or more persons fight`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did 2 or more persons (the accused among them) fight? (s 267A)
    `the accused is one of the persons fighting`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused one of those fighting? (s 267A)
    `in a public place`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the fight in a public place? (s 267A)
    `they disturb the public peace`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the fighting disturb the public peace? (s 267A)
    `the other persons`                      IS A STRING @desc The others who fought, as the charge is to name them
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@export Whether the accused "commits an affray" within section 267A of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Affray Facts` @desc Who fought, where, and what it did to the public peace
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits an affray` f IF
        "Where"
    AND f's `2 or more persons fight`
    AND f's `the accused is one of the persons fighting`
    AND f's `in a public place`
    AND f's `they disturb the public peace`
    AND "they are said to commit an affray"

§§ `s 267B - Punishment for committing affray`

-- 267B. Whoever commits an affray shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 267B
`punishment prescribed by s 267B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "267B"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 267B of the Penal Code 1871 (affray)
GIVEN f IS A `Affray Facts` @desc Who fought, where, and what it did to the public peace
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 267B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `commits an affray` f

@export Frame a charge under section 267B of the Penal Code 1871 (affray), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Affray Facts` @desc Who fought, where, and what it did to the public peace, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 267B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "267B" "affray"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 267B`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 267B` f)
        (CONCAT "together with ", f's `the other persons`, ", did disturb the public peace by fighting in a public place, and thereby commit an affray", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `2 or more persons fight`) "2 or more persons fight"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is one of the persons fighting`) "the accused is one of them"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in a public place`) "in a public place"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `they disturb the public peace`) "disturb the public peace"),
                (`missing unless` (`commits an affray` f) "the elements of section 267A taken together")))

§§ `s 267C - Uttering words, making document, etc., containing incitement to violence, etc.`

-- 267C.-(1) This section applies where a person -
--    (a) utters any words, or makes any sign or visible representation;
--    (b) places before a person any object;
--    (c) posts, publishes, distributes, sells or offers for sale any document; or
--    (d) communicates any electronic record, containing any incitement to violence,
--      counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant, or
--      likely to lead to any breach of the peace, and the person does so -
--    (e) intending for violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or
--      breach of the peace to occur; or
--    (f) knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience to the law or
--      such lawful order, or breach of the peace, is likely to occur as a result.
-- (2) This section also applies where a person -
--    (a) makes, prints or otherwise reproduces, imports, possesses or has under the
--      person's control any document mentioned in subsection (1), for the purpose of
--      posting, publishing, distributing, selling or offering for sale that document; or
--    (b) makes any electronic record mentioned in subsection (1) for the purpose of
--      communicating that electronic record, and the person does so -
--    (c) intending for violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or
--      breach of the peace to occur by the carrying out of the purpose mentioned in
--      paragraph (a) or (b), as the case may be; or
--    (d) knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience to the law or
--      such lawful order, or breach of the peace, is likely to occur by the carrying out
--      of that purpose.
-- (3) The person in subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- punished on conviction with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or
-- with fine, or with both.
-- (4) In subsection (1), "counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of
-- a public servant" includes (but is not limited to) providing instruction, advice or
-- information that promotes disobedience to the law or such order.
-- [Act 30 of 2021 wef 02/11/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 267C - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Incitement Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `utters any words, or makes any sign or visible representation`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(a))
    `places before a person any object`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(b))
    `posts, publishes, distributes, sells or offers for sale any document`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(c))
    `communicates any electronic record`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(d))
    `makes, prints, reproduces, imports, possesses or has under his control such a document for the purpose of posting, publishing, distributing, selling or offering it for sale`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(2)(a))
    `makes such an electronic record for the purpose of communicating it`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(2)(b))
    `containing any incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant, or likely to lead to any breach of the peace`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it contain incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant (which includes giving instruction, advice or information promoting such disobedience, s 267C(4)), or was it likely to lead to a breach of the peace? (s 267C(1))
    `intending for violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace to occur`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(e), (2)(c)) - a fault element
    `knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace is likely to occur as a result`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 267C(1)(f), (2)(d)) - a fault element
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 267C(3)
`punishment prescribed by s 267C` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "267C(3)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether section 267C(1) or (2) of the Penal Code 1871 applies to the accused
GIVEN f IS A `Incitement Facts` @desc What the accused uttered, placed, published or made, what it contained, and what the accused intended or knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `utters words or makes a document containing incitement to violence` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `utters any words, or makes any sign or visible representation` OR f's `places before a person any object` OR f's `posts, publishes, distributes, sells or offers for sale any document` OR f's `communicates any electronic record` OR f's `makes, prints, reproduces, imports, possesses or has under his control such a document for the purpose of posting, publishing, distributing, selling or offering it for sale` OR f's `makes such an electronic record for the purpose of communicating it`)
    AND f's `containing any incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant, or likely to lead to any breach of the peace`
    AND (f's `intending for violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace to occur` OR f's `knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace is likely to occur as a result`)

-- FORK JO-9: subsections (1) and (2) are read as one offence, punished by (3); the
-- (2)(c)-(d) mental elements ("by the carrying out of the purpose") share the
-- (1)(e)-(f) leaves.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 267C of the Penal Code 1871 (uttering words, making document, etc., containing incitement to violence)
GIVEN f IS A `Incitement Facts` @desc What the accused uttered, placed, published or made, what it contained, and what the accused intended or knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 267C` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `utters words or makes a document containing incitement to violence` f

@export Frame a charge under section 267C of the Penal Code 1871 (uttering words, making document, etc., containing incitement to violence), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Incitement Facts` @desc What the accused uttered, placed, published or made, what it contained, and what the accused intended or knew, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 267C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "267C" "uttering words, making document, etc., containing incitement to violence"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 267C`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 267C` f)
        (CONCAT "did utter words, publish a document or communicate an electronic record (or make or hold one for that purpose) containing incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law, or likely to lead to a breach of the peace, intending or knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience or a breach of the peace was likely to occur", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `utters any words, or makes any sign or visible representation` OR f's `places before a person any object` OR f's `posts, publishes, distributes, sells or offers for sale any document` OR f's `communicates any electronic record` OR f's `makes, prints, reproduces, imports, possesses or has under his control such a document for the purpose of posting, publishing, distributing, selling or offering it for sale` OR f's `makes such an electronic record for the purpose of communicating it`)) "utters words, places an object, publishes a document or communicates an electronic record (subsection (1)(a)-(d)), or makes or holds one for that purpose (subsection (2)(a)-(b))"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `containing any incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant, or likely to lead to any breach of the peace`) "containing any incitement to violence, counselling disobedience to the law or to a lawful order of a public servant, or likely to lead to any breach of the peace"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `intending for violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace to occur` OR f's `knowing or having reason to believe that violence, disobedience to the law or such lawful order, or breach of the peace is likely to occur as a result`)) "intending, or knowing or having reason to believe it likely, that violence, disobedience or breach of the peace will occur"),
                (`missing unless` (`utters words or makes a document containing incitement to violence` f) "the elements of section 267C taken together")))

§§ `s 268 - Public nuisance`

-- 268. A person is guilty of a public nuisance, who does any act, or is guilty of an
-- illegal omission, which causes any common injury, danger or annoyance to the public,
-- or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity, or which
-- must necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may
-- have occasion to use any public right.
-- Explanation.- A common nuisance is not excused on the ground that it causes some
-- convenience or advantage.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 268, 290, 291 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Public Nuisance Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `does any act or is guilty of an illegal omission`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do an act, or commit an illegal omission (s 43)? (s 268)
    `which causes any common injury, danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it cause common injury, danger or annoyance to the public, or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity? (s 268) - that it also causes some convenience or advantage is no excuse (Explanation)
    `which must necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may have occasion to use any public right`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must it necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may have occasion to use a public right? (s 268)
    `the case is not otherwise punishable by this Code`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the public nuisance NOT otherwise punishable by this Code? (s 290)
    `the offender knew that the act or omission will cause or will probably cause any common injury, danger or annoyance`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know the act or omission would (or would probably) cause common injury, danger or annoyance to the public or those in the vicinity? (s 290(b))
    `this is a second or subsequent conviction`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would this be the accused's second or subsequent conviction? (s 290(c))
    `having been enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority not to repeat or continue the nuisance`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had a public servant with lawful authority to do so enjoined the accused not to repeat or continue the nuisance? (s 291)
    `repeats or continues the public nuisance`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused repeat or continue the public nuisance? (s 291)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@export Whether the accused "is guilty of a public nuisance" within section 268 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is guilty of a public nuisance` f IF
        "A person is guilty of a public nuisance, who"
    AND f's `does any act or is guilty of an illegal omission`
    AND (    f's `which causes any common injury, danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity`
         OR  f's `which must necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may have occasion to use any public right` )

§§ `s 268A - Communicating false information of harmful thing`

-- 268A. Any person who transmits or communicates or causes to be transmitted or
-- communicated information -
--    (a) which contains a reference to the presence in any place or location or in any
--      conveyance or means of transportation of any thing that is likely to cause hurt
--      or damage to property by any means; and
--    (b) that person knows that such reference is false or fabricated, shall be guilty
--      of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $50,000, or with
--      both.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 268A-268C - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `transmits or communicates, or causes to be transmitted or communicated, information`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 268A)
    `which contains a reference to the presence in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation of any thing likely to cause hurt or damage to property`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 268A(a))
    `knows that such reference is false or fabricated`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 268A(b)) - a fault element
    `places any thing in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (ss 268B(1)(a), 268C(1)(a))
    `sends any thing from one place to another by post, courier or any other means`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (ss 268B(1)(b), 268C(1)(b))
    `without reasonable excuse`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it without reasonable excuse? (ss 268B, 268C)
    `with the intention of inducing in one or more other persons a belief that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 268B(1)) - no particular person need be in mind (s 268B(2))
    `does so intentionally`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the placing or sending intentional? (s 268C(1))
    `knowing that there is a real risk that one or more persons would believe that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 268C(1)) - no particular person need be in mind (s 268C(2))
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 268A
`punishment prescribed by s 268A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "268A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $50,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 50000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused communicates false information of a harmful thing (s 268A of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `communicates false information of a harmful thing` f IF
        "Any person who"
    AND f's `transmits or communicates, or causes to be transmitted or communicated, information`
    AND f's `which contains a reference to the presence in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation of any thing likely to cause hurt or damage to property`
    AND f's `knows that such reference is false or fabricated`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 268A of the Penal Code 1871 (communicating false information of harmful thing)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 268A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `communicates false information of a harmful thing` f

@export Frame a charge under section 268A of the Penal Code 1871 (communicating false information of harmful thing), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 268A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "268A" "communicating false information of harmful thing"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 268A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 268A` f)
        (CONCAT "did communicate information containing a reference to the presence of a thing likely to cause hurt or damage to property, knowing that reference to be false or fabricated", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `transmits or communicates, or causes to be transmitted or communicated, information`) "transmits or communicates, or causes to be transmitted or communicated, information"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `which contains a reference to the presence in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation of any thing likely to cause hurt or damage to property`) "(a) which contains a reference to the presence of any thing likely to cause hurt or damage to property"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows that such reference is false or fabricated`) "(b) knows that such reference is false or fabricated"),
                (`missing unless` (`communicates false information of a harmful thing` f) "the elements of section 268A taken together")))

§§ `s 268B - Placing or sending thing with intent to cause fear of harm`

-- 268B.-(1) Any person (A) who without reasonable excuse -
--    (a) places any thing in any place or location or in any conveyance or means of
--      transportation; or
--    (b) sends any thing from one place to another place by post, courier or any other
--      means, with the intention (in either case) of inducing in one or more other
--      persons a belief that this thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property by
--      any means, shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may
--      extend to $50,000, or with both.
-- [15/2019]
-- (2) For the purposes of subsection (1) and to avoid doubt, it is not necessary for A
-- to have any particular person or persons in mind as being induced to have the belief
-- mentioned in subsection (1).
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 268B(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 268B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "268B(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $50,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 50000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused places or sends a thing intending to induce a belief it is harmful (s 268B(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `places or sends a thing with intent to cause fear of harm` f IF
        "Any person who"
    AND f's `without reasonable excuse`
    AND (f's `places any thing in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation` OR f's `sends any thing from one place to another by post, courier or any other means`)
    AND f's `with the intention of inducing in one or more other persons a belief that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 268B of the Penal Code 1871 (placing or sending thing with intent to cause fear of harm)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 268B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `places or sends a thing with intent to cause fear of harm` f

@export Frame a charge under section 268B of the Penal Code 1871 (placing or sending thing with intent to cause fear of harm), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 268B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "268B" "placing or sending thing with intent to cause fear of harm"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 268B`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 268B` f)
        (CONCAT "did without reasonable excuse place or send a thing with the intention of inducing in others a belief that it was likely to cause hurt or damage to property", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `without reasonable excuse`) "without reasonable excuse"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `places any thing in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation` OR f's `sends any thing from one place to another by post, courier or any other means`)) "(a) places any thing in any place or conveyance, or (b) sends any thing by post, courier or other means"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention of inducing in one or more other persons a belief that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`) "with the intention of inducing in one or more other persons a belief that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property"),
                (`missing unless` (`places or sends a thing with intent to cause fear of harm` f) "the elements of section 268B taken together")))

§§ `s 268C - Placing or sending thing causing fear of harm`

-- 268C.-(1) Any person who intentionally and without reasonable excuse -
--    (a) places any thing in any place or location or in any conveyance or means of
--      transportation; or
--    (b) sends any thing from one place to another place by post, courier or any other
--      means, knowing that there is a real risk (in either case) that one or more
--      persons would believe that this thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to
--      property by any means, shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine
--      which may extend to $5,000, or with both.
-- [15/2019]
-- (2) To avoid doubt, it is not necessary for the accused person to have any
-- particular person or persons in mind as being at risk of having the belief mentioned
-- in subsection (1).
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 268C(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 268C` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "268C(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused intentionally places or sends a thing knowing of a real risk it will be believed harmful (s 268C(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `places or sends a thing causing fear of harm` f IF
        "Any person who"
    AND f's `does so intentionally`
    AND f's `without reasonable excuse`
    AND (f's `places any thing in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation` OR f's `sends any thing from one place to another by post, courier or any other means`)
    AND f's `knowing that there is a real risk that one or more persons would believe that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 268C of the Penal Code 1871 (placing or sending thing causing fear of harm)
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 268C` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `places or sends a thing causing fear of harm` f

@export Frame a charge under section 268C of the Penal Code 1871 (placing or sending thing causing fear of harm), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Harmful Thing Hoax Facts` @desc What the accused communicated, placed or sent, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 268C` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "268C" "placing or sending thing causing fear of harm"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 268C`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 268C` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally and without reasonable excuse place or send a thing, knowing that there was a real risk that others would believe it was likely to cause hurt or damage to property", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `does so intentionally`) "intentionally"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `without reasonable excuse`) "and without reasonable excuse"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `places any thing in any place, location, conveyance or means of transportation` OR f's `sends any thing from one place to another by post, courier or any other means`)) "(a) places any thing in any place or conveyance, or (b) sends any thing by post, courier or other means"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowing that there is a real risk that one or more persons would believe that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property`) "knowing that there is a real risk that one or more persons would believe that the thing is likely to cause hurt or damage to property"),
                (`missing unless` (`places or sends a thing causing fear of harm` f) "the elements of section 268C taken together")))

§§ `s 269 - Negligent act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life`

-- 269. Whoever unlawfully or negligently does any act which is, and which he knows or
-- has reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous
-- to life, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one
-- year, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 269-278 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Public Health Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `unlawfully or negligently`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done unlawfully (s 43) or negligently (s 26F)? (s 269)
    `intentionally or rashly`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done intentionally (s 26C) or rashly (s 26E)? (s 270)
    `does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act likely to spread the infection of a disease dangerous to life? (ss 269, 270)
    `knows or has reason to believe the act to be likely to spread the infection`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know, or have reason to believe, it was likely to spread the infection? (ss 269, 270) - a fault element
    `knowingly disobeys a rule lawfully made and promulgated for quarantine or for regulating intercourse with places where an infectious disease prevails`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused knowingly disobey a rule lawfully made and promulgated for putting a vessel into quarantine, regulating intercourse of quarantined vessels with the shore or other vessels, or regulating intercourse between places where an infectious disease prevails and other places? (s 271)
    `adulterates any article of food or drink so as to make it noxious as food or drink`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 272)
    `intending to sell it as food or drink, or knowing it likely to be sold as food or drink`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 272) - a fault element
    `sells, or offers or exposes for sale, as food or drink, an article which has been rendered or has become noxious or is unfit for food or drink`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 273)
    `knowing or having reason to believe that it is noxious as food or drink`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 273) - a fault element
    `adulterates any drug or medical preparation so as to lessen its efficacy, change its operation or make it noxious`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 274)
    `intending or knowing it likely that it will be sold or used for any medicinal purpose as if unadulterated`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 274) - a fault element
    `knowing a drug or medical preparation to have been so adulterated, sells, offers or exposes it for sale, issues it from a dispensary as unadulterated, or causes it to be used by a person not knowing of the adulteration`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 275)
    `knowingly sells, offers or exposes for sale, or issues from a dispensary, any drug or medical preparation as a different drug or medical preparation`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 276)
    `voluntarily corrupts or fouls the water of any public spring or reservoir so as to render it less fit for its ordinary purpose`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 277)
    `voluntarily vitiates the atmosphere in any place so as to make it noxious to the health of persons dwelling or carrying on business in the neighbourhood or passing along a public way`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 278)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 269
`punishment prescribed by s 269` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "269"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused unlawfully or negligently does an act likely to spread a dangerous infection (s 269 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `negligently does an act likely to spread infection` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `unlawfully or negligently`
    AND f's `does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life`
    AND f's `knows or has reason to believe the act to be likely to spread the infection`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 269 of the Penal Code 1871 (negligent act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 269` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `negligently does an act likely to spread infection` f

@export Frame a charge under section 269 of the Penal Code 1871 (negligent act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 269` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "269" "negligent act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 269`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 269` f)
        (CONCAT "did unlawfully or negligently do an act which was, and which you knew or had reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of a disease dangerous to life", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `unlawfully or negligently`) "unlawfully or negligently"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life`) "does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows or has reason to believe the act to be likely to spread the infection`) "which he knows or has reason to believe to be likely to spread the infection"),
                (`missing unless` (`negligently does an act likely to spread infection` f) "the elements of section 269 taken together")))

§§ `s 270 - Intentional or rash act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life`

-- 270. Whoever intentionally or rashly does any act which is, and which he knows or
-- has reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous
-- to life, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years,
-- or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 23 of 2021 wef 01/03/2022]

