GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 270` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "270" "intentional or rash act likely to spread infection of any disease dangerous to life"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 270`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 270` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally or rashly do an act which was, and which you knew or had reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of a disease dangerous to life", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `intentionally or rashly`) "intentionally or rashly"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life`) "does any act which is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `knows or has reason to believe the act to be likely to spread the infection`) "which he knows or has reason to believe to be likely to spread the infection"),
                (`missing unless` (`intentionally does an act likely to spread infection` f) "the elements of section 270 taken together")))

§§ `s 271 - Disobedience to a quarantine rule`

-- 271. Whoever knowingly disobeys any rule lawfully made and promulgated for putting
-- any vessel into a state of quarantine, or for regulating the intercourse of vessels
-- in a state of quarantine with the shore or with other vessels, or for regulating the
-- intercourse between places where an infectious disease prevails and other places,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 271
`punishment prescribed by s 271` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "271"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 271 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (disobedience to a quarantine rule)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disobeys a quarantine rule` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `knowingly disobeys a rule lawfully made and promulgated for quarantine or for regulating intercourse with places where an infectious disease prevails`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 271 of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to a quarantine rule)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 271` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `disobeys a quarantine rule` f

@export Frame a charge under section 271 of the Penal Code 1871 (disobedience to a quarantine rule), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 271` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "271" "disobedience to a quarantine rule"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 271`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 271` f)
        (CONCAT "did knowingly disobey a rule lawfully made and promulgated for quarantine", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowingly disobeys a rule lawfully made and promulgated for quarantine or for regulating intercourse with places where an infectious disease prevails`) "knowingly disobeys any rule lawfully made and promulgated for quarantine or for regulating intercourse with places where an infectious disease prevails"),
                (`missing unless` (`disobeys a quarantine rule` f) "the elements of section 271 taken together")))

§§ `s 272 - Adulteration of food or drink which is intended for sale`

-- 272. Whoever adulterates any article of food or drink, so as to make such article
-- noxious as food or drink, intending to sell such article as food or drink, or
-- knowing it to be likely that the same will be sold as food or drink, shall be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 272
`punishment prescribed by s 272` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "272"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

