                (`missing unless` (`sells noxious food or drink` f) "the elements of section 273 taken together")))

§§ `s 274 - Adulteration of drugs`

-- 274. Whoever adulterates any drug or medical preparation in such a manner as to
-- lessen the efficacy, or change the operation, of such drug or medical preparation,
-- or to make it noxious, intending that it shall be sold or used for, or knowing it to
-- be likely that it will be sold or used for any medicinal purpose, as if it had not
-- undergone such adulteration, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which
-- may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 274
`punishment prescribed by s 274` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "274"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 274 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (adulteration of drugs)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adulterates drugs` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `adulterates any drug or medical preparation so as to lessen its efficacy, change its operation or make it noxious`
    AND f's `intending or knowing it likely that it will be sold or used for any medicinal purpose as if unadulterated`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 274 of the Penal Code 1871 (adulteration of drugs)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 274` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `adulterates drugs` f

@export Frame a charge under section 274 of the Penal Code 1871 (adulteration of drugs), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Health Facts` @desc The act, the article, drug, water or air concerned, and what the accused knew or intended, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 274` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "274" "adulteration of drugs"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 274`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 274` f)
        (CONCAT "did adulterate a drug or medical preparation so as to lessen its efficacy, change its operation or make it noxious, intending or knowing it likely to be sold or used for a medicinal purpose as unadulterated", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `adulterates any drug or medical preparation so as to lessen its efficacy, change its operation or make it noxious`) "adulterates any drug or medical preparation in such a manner as to lessen its efficacy, change its operation, or make it noxious"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intending or knowing it likely that it will be sold or used for any medicinal purpose as if unadulterated`) "intending that it shall be sold or used for, or knowing it likely that it will be sold or used for, any medicinal purpose, as if it had not undergone such adulteration"),
                (`missing unless` (`adulterates drugs` f) "the elements of section 274 taken together")))

§§ `s 275 - Sale of adulterated drugs`

-- 275. Whoever, knowing any drug or medical preparation to have been adulterated in
-- such a manner as to lessen its efficacy, to change its operation, or to render it
-- noxious, sells the same, or offers or exposes it for sale, or issues it from any
-- dispensary for medicinal purposes as unadulterated, or causes it to be used for
-- medicinal purposes by any person not knowing of the adulteration, shall be punished
-- with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with
-- both.
-- [15/2019]

