§§ `s 279 - Rash driving or riding on a public way`

-- 279. Whoever drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way, in a manner so rash or
-- negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any
-- other person, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one
-- year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 279-283 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Rash Conduct Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 279)
    `navigates any vessel`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 280)
    `in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done so rashly (s 26E) or negligently (s 26F) as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to another? (ss 279, 280)
    `exhibits any false light, mark or buoy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 281)
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that such exhibition will mislead any navigator`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 281) - a fault element
    `knowingly or negligently conveys, or causes to be conveyed, for hire any person by water in a vessel`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 282)
    `when the vessel is in such a state or so loaded as to endanger the life of that person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 282)
    `by doing any act, or by omitting to take order with any property in his possession or under his charge, causes danger, obstruction or injury to any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 283)
    `in any public way or public line of navigation`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 283)
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 279
`punishment prescribed by s 279` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "279"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused commits the acts section 279 of the Penal Code 1871 describes (rash driving or riding on a public way)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused drove, rode or navigated, how, and with what danger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `drives rashly on a public way` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way`
    AND f's `in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 279 of the Penal Code 1871 (rash driving or riding on a public way)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused drove, rode or navigated, how, and with what danger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 279` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `drives rashly on a public way` f

@export Frame a charge under section 279 of the Penal Code 1871 (rash driving or riding on a public way), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused drove, rode or navigated, how, and with what danger, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 279` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "279" "rash driving or riding on a public way"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 279`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 279` f)
        (CONCAT "did drive a vehicle, or ride, on a public way in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to another person", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way`) "drives any vehicle, or rides, on any public way"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person`) "in a manner so rash or negligent as to endanger human life, or to be likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person"),
                (`missing unless` (`drives rashly on a public way` f) "the elements of section 279 taken together")))

