@export Whether the accused does an act with a dangerous or harmful substance so rashly or negligently as section 284(1) of the Penal Code 1871 describes
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does a rash act with a dangerous substance` f IF
        "A person shall be guilty of an offence who"
    AND f's `does any act with any dangerous or harmful substance`
    AND f's `so rashly or negligently`
    AND (f's `likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person` OR f's `endangers human life` OR f's `causes hurt or injury to any other person` OR f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` OR f's `causes the death of any other person`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 284 of the Penal Code 1871 (rash or negligent conduct with respect to dangerous or harmful substance)
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 284` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `does a rash act with a dangerous substance` f

@export Frame a charge under section 284 of the Penal Code 1871 (rash or negligent conduct with respect to dangerous or harmful substance), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 284` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "284" "rash or negligent conduct with respect to dangerous or harmful substance"
        (IF f's `causes the death of any other person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 284(3)(d)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 284(3)(c)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `causes hurt or injury to any other person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 284(3)(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 284(3)(a)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 284` f)
        (CONCAT "did an act with a dangerous or harmful substance so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or to be likely to cause, or to cause, hurt, grievous hurt or death to another person", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `does any act with any dangerous or harmful substance`) "does, with any dangerous or harmful substance, any act"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `so rashly or negligently`) "so rashly or negligently"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person` OR f's `endangers human life` OR f's `causes hurt or injury to any other person` OR f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` OR f's `causes the death of any other person`)) "with one of the results the subsection lists"),
                (`missing unless` (`does a rash act with a dangerous substance` f) "the elements of section 284 taken together")))

§§ `s 285 - Causing or contributing to risk of dangerous fire`

-- 285.-(1) Whoever, with any fire or any thing that is likely to cause fire, rashly or
-- negligently causes or substantially contributes to the risk of causing a fire, shall
-- be guilty of an offence if such fire occurs and any of the following applies:
--    (a) that fire is likely to cause hurt or injury to any other person;
--    (b) that fire endangers human life;
--    (c) that fire causes damage to or diminishes the value or utility of any property
--      belonging to any other person or the Government;
--    (d) that fire causes hurt or injury to any other person;
--    (e) that fire causes grievous hurt to any other person;
--    (f) that fire causes death to any other person.
-- [15/2019]
-- (2) Any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall on conviction
-- be punished -
--    (a) in the case of an offence under subsection (1)(a) or (b), with imprisonment
--      for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000,
--      or with both;
--    (b) in the case of an offence under subsection (1)(c), with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 18 months, or with fine, or with both;
--    (c) in the case of an offence under subsection (1)(d), with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both;
--    (d) in the case of an offence under subsection (1)(e), with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 6 years, or with fine, or with both; and
--    (e) in the case of an offence under subsection (1)(f), with imprisonment for a
--      term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [15/2019]

@export Whether a person is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have substantially contributed to the risk of causing a fire (s 286 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is presumed to have substantially contributed to the risk of fire within section 286` f IF
        "In any proceedings for an offence under section 285, where any person"
    AND f's `deposits, drops, places or throws a cigarette, cigar, match stick, charcoal, incense, embers or any thing likely to cause fire in a place`
    AND "and"
    AND f's `a fire occurs at or in the vicinity of that place within 60 minutes from the time of that act`
    AND "that person is, until the contrary is proved, presumed to have substantially contributed to the risk of causing that fire"
    AND NOT f's `the contrary is proved`

@export Whether a fire occurred "within 60 minutes from the time of that act" (s 286 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN minutes IS A NUMBER @desc The minutes between the act and the fire
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within 60 minutes` minutes IF minutes AT MOST 60

