@export Whether the accused omits sufficient precautions with an animal, with a result section 289(1) of the Penal Code 1871 lists
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `omits precautions with an animal` f IF
        "A person shall be guilty of an offence who"
    AND f's `knowingly or negligently omits to take sufficient measure with any animal against probable danger to human life or of grievous hurt from it`
    AND (f's `is likely to cause grievous hurt` OR f's `endangers human life` OR f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` OR f's `causes the death of any other person`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 289 of the Penal Code 1871 (negligence with respect to any animal)
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 289` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `omits precautions with an animal` f

@export Frame a charge under section 289 of the Penal Code 1871 (negligence with respect to any animal), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Dangerous Conduct Facts` @desc What the accused did or omitted with a substance, fire, machinery, building or animal, how, and with what result, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 289` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "289" "negligence with respect to any animal"
        (IF f's `causes the death of any other person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 289(2)(c)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 289(2)(b)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 289(2)(a)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 289` f)
        (CONCAT "did knowingly or negligently omit to take sufficient measures with an animal against probable danger to human life or of grievous hurt, which omission endangered human life or was likely to cause, or caused, grievous hurt or death", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `knowingly or negligently omits to take sufficient measure with any animal against probable danger to human life or of grievous hurt from it`) "knowingly or negligently omits to take such measure with any animal as is sufficient to guard against probable danger to human life or of grievous hurt"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `is likely to cause grievous hurt` OR f's `endangers human life` OR f's `causes grievous hurt to any other person` OR f's `causes the death of any other person`)) "with one of the results the subsection lists"),
                (`missing unless` (`omits precautions with an animal` f) "the elements of section 289 taken together")))

§§ `s 290 - Punishment for public nuisance`

-- 290. Whoever commits a public nuisance in any case not otherwise punishable by this
-- Code, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be punished -
--    (a) with fine which may extend to $2,000;
--    (b) in the case where the offender knew that the act or omission constituting the
--      public nuisance will cause or will probably cause any common injury, danger or
--      annoyance to the public, or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property
--      in the vicinity, with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or
--      with fine which may extend to $2,000, or with both; or
--    (c) on a second or subsequent conviction, with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,000, or with both.
-- [15/2019]

-- Paragraph (a) is the base; (b) (knowledge) and (c) (a second or subsequent
-- conviction) share one heavier punishment. A charge picks (b) or (c) where their leaf
-- holds.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 290(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 290(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "290(a)"
    words                    IS "fine which may extend to $2,000"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 290(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 290(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "290(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 290(c)
`punishment prescribed by s 290(c)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "290(c)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 290 of the Penal Code 1871 (public nuisance)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 290` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `is guilty of a public nuisance` f
    AND f's `the case is not otherwise punishable by this Code`

@export Frame a charge under section 290 of the Penal Code 1871 (public nuisance), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 290` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "290" "public nuisance"
        (IF f's `the offender knew that the act or omission will cause or will probably cause any common injury, danger or annoyance` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 290(b)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `this is a second or subsequent conviction` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 290(c)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 290(a)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 290` f)
        (CONCAT "did commit a public nuisance", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `does any act or is guilty of an illegal omission`) "does any act or is guilty of an illegal omission"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `which causes any common injury, danger or annoyance to the public or to the people in general who dwell or occupy property in the vicinity` OR f's `which must necessarily cause injury, obstruction, danger or annoyance to persons who may have occasion to use any public right`)) "which causes common injury, danger or annoyance to the public, or must necessarily cause it to persons using a public right"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the case is not otherwise punishable by this Code`) "in any case not otherwise punishable by this Code"),
                (`missing unless` (`is guilty of a public nuisance` f) "the elements of section 268 taken together")))

§§ `s 291 - Continuance of nuisance after injunction to discontinue`

-- 291. Whoever repeats or continues a public nuisance, having been enjoined by any
-- public servant who has lawful authority to issue such injunction not to repeat or
-- continue such nuisance, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 291
`punishment prescribed by s 291` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "291"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused repeats or continues a public nuisance after being enjoined by a public servant not to (s 291 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `continues a public nuisance after injunction` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `repeats or continues the public nuisance`
    AND `is guilty of a public nuisance` f
    AND f's `having been enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority not to repeat or continue the nuisance`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 291 of the Penal Code 1871 (continuance of nuisance after injunction to discontinue)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 291` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `continues a public nuisance after injunction` f

@export Frame a charge under section 291 of the Penal Code 1871 (continuance of nuisance after injunction to discontinue), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Nuisance Facts` @desc The act or omission, what it did to the public, and what the accused knew, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 291` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "291" "continuance of nuisance after injunction to discontinue"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 291`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 291` f)
        (CONCAT "having been enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority not to repeat or continue a public nuisance, did repeat or continue that nuisance", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `repeats or continues the public nuisance`) "repeats or continues a public nuisance"),
                (`missing unless` (`is guilty of a public nuisance` f) "a public nuisance (section 268)"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `having been enjoined by a public servant with lawful authority not to repeat or continue the nuisance`) "having been enjoined by any public servant who has lawful authority to issue such injunction not to repeat or continue such nuisance"),
                (`missing unless` (`continues a public nuisance after injunction` f) "the elements of section 291 taken together")))

§§ `s 292 - Sale of obscene objects, etc.`

-- 292.-(1) Whoever -
--    (a) sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or puts into circulation
--      any obscene object by any means (electronic or otherwise);
--    (b) makes, produces or has in his possession any obscene object for the purposes
--      of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation of such object by
--      any means (electronic or otherwise);
--    (c) imports, exports or conveys any obscene object -
--    (i) for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or
--      circulation of such object by any means (electronic or otherwise); or
--    (ii) knowing or having reason to believe that such object will be sold, let to
--      hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or put into circulation by any means
--      (electronic or otherwise);
--    (d) takes part in, or receives profits from, any business in the course of which
--      he knows or has reason to believe that any obscene object is -
--    (i) made, produced, purchased, kept, imported, exported or conveyed for the
--      purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation of such
--      object by any means (electronic or otherwise); or
--    (ii) sold, let to hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or put into circulation,
--      by any means (electronic or otherwise);
--    (e) advertises, or makes known by any means whatsoever, that any person is
--      engaged or is ready to engage in any act which is an offence under this section,
--      or that any obscene object can be procured from or through any person; or
--    (f) offers or attempts to do any act which is an offence under this section,
--      shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (1A) Subject to subsection (1B)(a), a person who is guilty of an offence under
-- subsection (1) shall, in the following cases be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both:
--    (a) for an offence under subsection (1)(a) - if the person sells, lets to hire,
--      distributes, publicly exhibits or circulates, by electronic means, the obscene
--      object to 10 or more individuals;
--    (b) for an offence under subsection (1)(b) - if the person makes, produces or has
--      in his possession the obscene object for the purposes of sale, hire,
--      distribution, public exhibition or circulation of such object by electronic
--      means, to 10 or more individuals;
--    (c) for an offence under subsection (1)(c)(i) - if the person imports, exports or
--      conveys the obscene object for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public
--      exhibition or circulation of such object by electronic means, to 10 or more
--      individuals;
--    (d) for an offence under subsection (1)(c)(ii) - if the person imports, exports
--      or conveys the obscene object knowing or having reason to believe that such
--      object will be sold, let to hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or circulated,
--      by electronic means, to 10 or more individuals;
--    (e) for an offence under subsection (1)(d)(i) - if the person takes part in, or
--      receives profits from, any business in the course of which he knows or has reason
--      to believe that any such obscene object is made, produced, purchased, kept,
--      imported, exported or conveyed, for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution,
--      public exhibition or circulation of such object by electronic means, to 10 or
--      more individuals;
--    (f) for an offence under subsection (1)(d)(ii) - if the person takes part in, or
--      receives profits from, any business in the course of which he knows or has reason
--      to believe that any such obscene object is sold, let to hire, distributed,
--      publicly exhibited or put into circulation, by electronic means, to 10 or more
--      individuals;
--    (g) for an offence under subsection (1)(e) - if the person advertises, or makes
--      known by any means whatsoever, that -
--    (i) any person is engaged or is ready to engage in any act mentioned in paragraph
--      (a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) which is an offence under subsection (1)(a), (b),
--      (c) or (d); or
--    (ii) any such obscene object can be procured from or through any person for the
--      purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation, by
--      electronic means, to 10 or more individuals;
--    (h) for an offence under subsection (1)(f) - if the person offers or attempts to
--      do any act mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f) or (g) which is an
--      offence under subsection (1)(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e).
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (1B) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) in the case where the
-- obscene object mentioned in that subsection depicts an image of a person who is, or
-- who appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of
-- age -
--    (a) in the case of any offence under subsection (1)(a), (b), (c), (d), (e) or (f)
--      for any act mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (h) of
--      subsection (1A) - shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
--      to 4 years, and shall also be liable to a fine; or
--    (b) in any other case - shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (1C) Whoever, on 2 or more occasions, sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly
-- exhibits or puts into circulation, by electronic means, any obscene object, to a
-- total number of 10 or more individuals, shall be guilty of an offence and on
-- conviction -
--    (a) if the obscene object depicts an image of a person who is, or who appears to
--      a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age - shall
--      be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, and shall
--      also be liable to a fine; or
--    (b) in any other case - shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (2) For the purposes of this section and sections 292B and 293 -
-- "object" includes data stored in a computer disc, or by other electronic means, that
-- is capable of conversion to images, writing or any other form of representation;
-- "obscene object" means any obscene book, pamphlet, paper, drawing, painting,
-- representation or figure, or any other obscene object whatsoever.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]
-- (3) For the purposes of this section and sections 292B and 293, an object shall be
-- deemed not to be obscene if the sale, letting to hire, distribution, exhibition,
-- circulation, import, export or conveyance of, or any other dealing in, the object is
-- authorised by or under any written law.
-- Exception.- This section and section 292B do not extend to any book, pamphlet,
-- writing, drawing or painting kept or used bona fide for religious purposes, or any
-- representation sculptured, engraved, painted or otherwise represented on or in any
-- temple, or on any car used for the conveyance of idols, or kept or used for any
-- religious purpose.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]

-- FORK JO-10: s 292(1) is one offence with limbs (a)-(f); (1A) and (1B) raise its
-- punishment where the dealing is electronic to 10 or more individuals, or the object
-- depicts a person below 18. The charge picks the punishment from those two leaves.
-- Paragraph-by-paragraph pairing of (1A)(a)-(h) with (1)(a)-(f) is collapsed into one
-- leaf.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 292-294 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Obscenity Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the object is an obscene object`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an obscene object - an obscene book, pamphlet, paper, drawing, painting, representation or figure, or any other obscene object, including data capable of conversion into images or writing (s 292(2))? It is deemed not obscene if the dealing is authorised by or under written law (s 292(3), the next leaf).
    `the dealing is authorised by or under any written law`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dealing in the object authorised by or under written law? If so it is deemed not obscene (s 292(3), for ss 292, 292B and 293)
    `the object is kept or used bona fide for religious purposes`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a book, pamphlet, writing, drawing or painting kept or used bona fide for religious purposes, or a representation on or in a temple, an idol car, or kept or used for a religious purpose? (Exception to ss 292 and 292B)
    `sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or puts into circulation the obscene object`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(a))
    `makes, produces or has in his possession the obscene object for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(b))
    `imports, exports or conveys the obscene object for those purposes, or knowing or having reason to believe it will be so dealt with`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(c))
    `takes part in, or receives profits from, a business in which he knows or has reason to believe obscene objects are so made or dealt with`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(d))
    `advertises or makes known that a person is engaged or ready to engage in such an act, or that an obscene object can be procured from or through any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(e))
    `offers or attempts to do any such act`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1)(f))
    `by electronic means, to 10 or more individuals`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done (or for the purpose of being done) by electronic means to 10 or more individuals? (s 292(1A)) - the helper `10 or more individuals` decides it from the count
    `the object depicts an image of a person who is, appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (ss 292(1B), 292(1C)(a), 292B(2)) - the helper `below 18 years of age` decides it from an age
    `on 2 or more occasions, sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or circulates by electronic means an obscene object to a total of 10 or more individuals`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292(1C))
    `imports, exports, conveys, sells, lets to hire, distributes, puts into circulation, makes, produces or is in possession of a child sex-doll`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused so deal in a child sex-doll - an anatomically correct doll, mannequin or robot with the features of (or appearing to a reasonable observer to resemble) a person below 16 years of age, intended for use in sexual activities (s 292A(2))? (s 292A(1))
    `an obscene object is sold, let for hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292B(1)) - "online location" is an internet domain, website, webpage, chatroom, channel, group, forum or other internet location (s 292B(3))
    `develops, maintains, organises, manages, supervises, regulates membership of or access to, or exercises editorial control over, the online location`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292B(1)(a)(i)-(iv)) - whether or not the person provides the online service
    `intended that the online location be used to enable or facilitate the sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation of obscene objects generally`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 292B(1)(b))
    `sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates, or offers or attempts to do so, an obscene object to a person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 293)
    `the person is below 21 years of age`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person below 21 years of age? (s 293) - the helper `below 21 years of age` decides it from the age
    `to the annoyance of others`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done to the annoyance of others? (s 294)
    `does any obscene act in any public place`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 294(a))
    `sings, recites or utters any obscene words in or near any public place`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 294(b))
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@export Whether a number of individuals is "10 or more individuals" (ss 292(1A), 292(1C), 292B(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER @desc The number of individuals
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `10 or more individuals` n IF n AT LEAST 10

@export Whether an object is an "obscene object" for sections 292, 292B and 293 of the Penal Code 1871, read with s 292(3) and the Exception
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the object is obscene within section 292` f IF
        f's `the object is an obscene object`
    AND NOT f's `the dealing is authorised by or under any written law`
    AND NOT f's `the object is kept or used bona fide for religious purposes`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1A)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1A)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1A)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1B)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1B)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1B)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, and shall also be liable to a fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 48
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1B)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1B)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1B)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused does any act in section 292(1)(a) to (f) of the Penal Code 1871 with an obscene object
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `deals in an obscene object` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `the object is obscene within section 292` f
    AND (f's `sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or puts into circulation the obscene object` OR f's `makes, produces or has in his possession the obscene object for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation` OR f's `imports, exports or conveys the obscene object for those purposes, or knowing or having reason to believe it will be so dealt with` OR f's `takes part in, or receives profits from, a business in which he knows or has reason to believe obscene objects are so made or dealt with` OR f's `advertises or makes known that a person is engaged or ready to engage in such an act, or that an obscene object can be procured from or through any person` OR f's `offers or attempts to do any such act`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 292 of the Penal Code 1871 (sale of obscene objects)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 292` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `deals in an obscene object` f

@export Frame a charge under section 292 of the Penal Code 1871 (sale of obscene objects), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 292` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "292" "sale of obscene objects"
        (IF f's `the object depicts an image of a person who is, appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age` AND f's `by electronic means, to 10 or more individuals` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1B)(a)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `the object depicts an image of a person who is, appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1B)(b)`)'s words ELSE IF f's `by electronic means, to 10 or more individuals` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1A)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 292` f)
        (CONCAT "did sell, distribute, exhibit, circulate, make, possess, import, export or convey, or deal in, an obscene object, or offer or attempt to do so", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (`the object is obscene within section 292` f) "any obscene object (subsections (2), (3) and the Exception)"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or puts into circulation the obscene object` OR f's `makes, produces or has in his possession the obscene object for the purposes of sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation` OR f's `imports, exports or conveys the obscene object for those purposes, or knowing or having reason to believe it will be so dealt with` OR f's `takes part in, or receives profits from, a business in which he knows or has reason to believe obscene objects are so made or dealt with` OR f's `advertises or makes known that a person is engaged or ready to engage in such an act, or that an obscene object can be procured from or through any person` OR f's `offers or attempts to do any such act`)) "does any act in paragraphs (a) to (f) of subsection (1)"),
                (`missing unless` (`deals in an obscene object` f) "the elements of section 292 taken together")))

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 292(1C) of the Penal Code 1871 (distributing obscene objects electronically on 2 or more occasions to 10 or more individuals)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 292(1C)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `on 2 or more occasions, sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or circulates by electronic means an obscene object to a total of 10 or more individuals`
    AND `the object is obscene within section 292` f

@export Frame a charge under section 292(1C) of the Penal Code 1871 ("distributing obscene objects by electronic means on 2 or more occasions"), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 292(1C)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "292(1C)" "distributing obscene objects by electronic means on 2 or more occasions"
        (IF f's `the object depicts an image of a person who is, appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1C)(a)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 292(1C)(b)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 292(1C)` f)
        (CONCAT "did on 2 or more occasions sell, distribute, exhibit or circulate by electronic means an obscene object to a total of 10 or more individuals", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `on 2 or more occasions, sells, lets to hire, distributes, publicly exhibits or circulates by electronic means an obscene object to a total of 10 or more individuals`) "on 2 or more occasions, by electronic means, to a total number of 10 or more individuals"),
                (`missing unless` (`the object is obscene within section 292` f) "any obscene object")))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1C)(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1C)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1C)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, and shall also be liable to a fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 48
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292(1C)(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 292(1C)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292(1C)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

§§ `s 292A - Possession, distribution, etc., of child sex-doll`

-- 292A.-(1) Any person who imports, exports, conveys, sells, lets to hire,
-- distributes, puts into circulation, makes, produces or is in possession of a child
-- sex-doll shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [15/2019]
-- (2) In subsection (1), "child sex-doll" means an anatomically correct doll,
-- mannequin or robot, with the features of, or with features that appear to a
-- reasonable observer to resemble a person below 16 years of age and intended for use
-- in sexual activities.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292A(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 292A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292A(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused deals in or possesses a child sex-doll (s 292A(1) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `deals in a child sex-doll` f IF
        "Any person who"
    AND f's `imports, exports, conveys, sells, lets to hire, distributes, puts into circulation, makes, produces or is in possession of a child sex-doll`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 292A of the Penal Code 1871 (possession, distribution, etc., of child sex-doll)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 292A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `deals in a child sex-doll` f

@export Frame a charge under section 292A of the Penal Code 1871 (possession, distribution, etc., of child sex-doll), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 292A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "292A" "possession, distribution, etc., of child sex-doll"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 292A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 292A` f)
        (CONCAT "did import, export, convey, sell, distribute, make, produce or possess a child sex-doll", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `imports, exports, conveys, sells, lets to hire, distributes, puts into circulation, makes, produces or is in possession of a child sex-doll`) "imports, exports, conveys, sells, lets to hire, distributes, puts into circulation, makes, produces or is in possession of a child sex-doll"),
                (`missing unless` (`deals in a child sex-doll` f) "the elements of section 292A taken together")))

§§ `s 292B - Obscene object on online location`

-- 292B.-(1) If any obscene object is sold, let for hire, distributed, publicly
-- exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location, any person
-- -
--    (a) who (whether or not the person provides an online service on or through which
--      the online location can be accessed) -
--    (i) develops and maintains the online location;
--    (ii) organises, manages or supervises the use of the online location;
--    (iii) manages or regulates membership of, or access to, the online location; or
--    (iv) has the authority to decide whether any material may be included or excluded
--      on the online location, or where to place the material on the online location or
--      otherwise exercise editorial control over the online location; and
--    (b) who, in doing the act mentioned in paragraph (a), intended that the online
--      location be used to enable or facilitate the sale, hire, distribution, public
--      exhibition or circulation of obscene objects generally, shall be guilty of an
--      offence and shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5
--      years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) in the case where the
-- obscene object mentioned in that subsection depicts an image of a person who is, or
-- who appears to a reasonable observer to be, or who is implied to be, below 18 years
-- of age shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years,
-- and shall also be liable to fine.
-- (3) In this section -
-- "online location" means any internet domain, website, webpage, chatroom, channel,
-- group, forum or any other location, that can be accessed by means of the Internet;
-- "online service" means the whole or any part of any service on or through which
-- online activity can be conducted and which can be accessed by means of the Internet.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292B(1)
`punishment prescribed by s 292B(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292B(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 292B(2)
`punishment prescribed by s 292B(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "292B(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused is liable under section 292B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 for an online location used to circulate obscene objects
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `runs an online location for obscene objects` f IF
        "any person"
    AND f's `an obscene object is sold, let for hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location`
    AND `the object is obscene within section 292` f
    AND f's `develops, maintains, organises, manages, supervises, regulates membership of or access to, or exercises editorial control over, the online location`
    AND f's `intended that the online location be used to enable or facilitate the sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation of obscene objects generally`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 292B of the Penal Code 1871 (obscene object on online location)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 292B` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `runs an online location for obscene objects` f

@export Frame a charge under section 292B of the Penal Code 1871 (obscene object on online location), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 292B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "292B" "obscene object on online location"
        (IF f's `the object depicts an image of a person who is, appears to a reasonable observer to be, or is implied to be, below 18 years of age` THEN (`punishment prescribed by s 292B(2)`)'s words ELSE (`punishment prescribed by s 292B(1)`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 292B` f)
        (CONCAT "did develop, maintain, manage or control an online location on which an obscene object was circulated to 10 or more individuals, intending that it be used to facilitate the circulation of obscene objects generally", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `an obscene object is sold, let for hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location`) "if any obscene object is sold, let for hire, distributed, publicly exhibited or circulated to 10 or more individuals on an online location"),
                (`missing unless` (`the object is obscene within section 292` f) "obscene object (section 292(2), (3) and the Exception)"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `develops, maintains, organises, manages, supervises, regulates membership of or access to, or exercises editorial control over, the online location`) "(a) develops and maintains, organises, manages or supervises, manages membership of or access to, or exercises editorial control over the online location"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `intended that the online location be used to enable or facilitate the sale, hire, distribution, public exhibition or circulation of obscene objects generally`) "(b) intended that the online location be used to enable or facilitate the circulation of obscene objects generally"),
                (`missing unless` (`runs an online location for obscene objects` f) "the elements of section 292B taken together")))

§§ `s 293 - Sale, etc., of obscene objects to young person`

-- 293. Whoever sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates to any person
-- below 21 years of age any obscene object as defined in section 292(2), or offers or
-- attempts to do so, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- to one year, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 21 of 2025 wef 17/08/2026] Obscene acts

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 293
`punishment prescribed by s 293` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "293"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused sells, distributes or exhibits an obscene object to a person below 21 (s 293 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `deals in an obscene object with a young person` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates, or offers or attempts to do so, an obscene object to a person`
    AND f's `the person is below 21 years of age`
    AND `the object is obscene within section 292` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 293 of the Penal Code 1871 (sale, etc., of obscene objects to young person)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 293` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `deals in an obscene object with a young person` f

@export Frame a charge under section 293 of the Penal Code 1871 (sale, etc., of obscene objects to young person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 293` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "293" "sale, etc., of obscene objects to young person"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 293`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 293` f)
        (CONCAT "did sell, distribute, exhibit or circulate an obscene object to a person below 21 years of age, or offer or attempt to do so", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates, or offers or attempts to do so, an obscene object to a person`) "sells, lets to hire, distributes, exhibits or circulates, or offers or attempts to do so"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `the person is below 21 years of age`) "to any person below 21 years of age"),
                (`missing unless` (`the object is obscene within section 292` f) "any obscene object as defined in section 292(2)"),
                (`missing unless` (`deals in an obscene object with a young person` f) "the elements of section 293 taken together")))

§§ `s 294 - Obscene acts Chapter 15 - Offences relating to race`

-- 294. Whoever, to the annoyance of others -
--    (a) does any obscene act in any public place; or
--    (b) sings, recites or utters any obscene words in or near any public place, shall
--      be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with
--      fine, or with both.
-- [15/2019]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 294
`punishment prescribed by s 294` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "294"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, to the annoyance of others, does an obscene act or utters obscene words in or near a public place (s 294 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does an obscene act in a public place` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `to the annoyance of others`
    AND (f's `does any obscene act in any public place` OR f's `sings, recites or utters any obscene words in or near any public place`)

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 294 of the Penal Code 1871 (obscene acts)
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 294` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `does an obscene act in a public place` f

@export Frame a charge under section 294 of the Penal Code 1871 (obscene acts), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Obscenity Facts` @desc The object, act or words, what the accused did with them, and to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 294` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "294" "obscene acts"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 294`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 294` f)
        (CONCAT "did, to the annoyance of others, do an obscene act in a public place, or sing, recite or utter obscene words in or near a public place", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `to the annoyance of others`) "to the annoyance of others"),
                (`missing unless` ((f's `does any obscene act in any public place` OR f's `sings, recites or utters any obscene words in or near any public place`)) "(a) does any obscene act in any public place, or (b) sings, recites or utters any obscene words in or near any public place"),
                (`missing unless` (`does an obscene act in a public place` f) "the elements of section 294 taken together")))

§ `Chapter 15 - Offences relating to race`

-- s 295. [Repealed by Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022]

-- s 296. [Repealed by Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022]

-- s 297. [Repealed by Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022]

§§ `s 298 - Uttering words, etc., with deliberate intent to wound the racial feelings of any person`

-- 298. Whoever, with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of any
-- person, utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing of that person, or makes
-- any gesture in the sight of that person, or places any object in the sight of that
-- person, or causes any matter however represented to be seen or heard by that person,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.
-- [Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022] Promoting enmity between different groups on grounds
-- of race and doing acts prejudicial to maintenance of harmony

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 298, 298A - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Racial Feelings Facts` HAS
    particulars                              IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of any person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 298) - a fault element
    `utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing of that person, makes any gesture or places any object in the sight of that person, or causes any matter to be seen or heard by that person`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 298)
    `by words, signs, visible representations or otherwise, knowingly promotes or attempts to promote, on grounds of race, disharmony or feelings of enmity, hatred or ill will between different racial groups`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 298A(a))
    `commits any act which he knows is prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different racial groups`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 298A(b))
    `which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility`
                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc (s 298A(b))
    `the person`                             IS A STRING @desc The person whose racial feelings were to be wounded (s 298), as the charge is to name them
    `what was done`                          IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read in the charge after "to wit,"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 298
`punishment prescribed by s 298` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "298"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, with deliberate intention of wounding a person's racial feelings, utters words or makes sounds, gestures or objects perceptible to that person (s 298 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wounds the racial feelings of a person` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of any person`
    AND f's `utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing of that person, makes any gesture or places any object in the sight of that person, or causes any matter to be seen or heard by that person`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 298 of the Penal Code 1871 (uttering words, etc., with deliberate intent to wound the racial feelings of any person)
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 298` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `wounds the racial feelings of a person` f

@export Frame a charge under section 298 of the Penal Code 1871 (uttering words, etc., with deliberate intent to wound the racial feelings of any person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 298` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "298" "uttering words, etc., with deliberate intent to wound the racial feelings of any person"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 298`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 298` f)
        (CONCAT "did, with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of one ", f's `the person`, ", utter words or make sounds in the hearing of, or make gestures or place objects in the sight of, that person", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` (f's `with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of any person`) "with deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of any person"),
                (`missing unless` (f's `utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing of that person, makes any gesture or places any object in the sight of that person, or causes any matter to be seen or heard by that person`) "utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing, or makes any gesture or places any object in the sight, of that person, or causes any matter to be seen or heard by that person"),
                (`missing unless` (`wounds the racial feelings of a person` f) "the elements of section 298 taken together")))

§§ `s 298A - Promoting enmity between different groups on grounds of race and doing acts prejudicial to maintenance of harmony Chapter 16 - Offences affecting the human body Offences affecting life`

-- 298A. Whoever -
--    (a) by words, either spoken or written, or by signs or by visible representations
--      or otherwise, knowingly promotes or attempts to promote, on grounds of race,
--      disharmony or feelings of enmity, hatred or ill will between different racial
--      groups; or
-- [Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022]
--    (b) commits any act which he knows is prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony
--      between different racial groups and which disturbs or is likely to disturb the
--      public tranquility, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- [Act 31 of 2019 wef 01/11/2022]

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 298A
`punishment prescribed by s 298A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "298A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused promotes racial enmity (s 298A(a)) or knowingly commits an act prejudicial to racial harmony that disturbs public tranquility (s 298A(b)) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `promotes enmity between racial groups` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (f's `by words, signs, visible representations or otherwise, knowingly promotes or attempts to promote, on grounds of race, disharmony or feelings of enmity, hatred or ill will between different racial groups` OR (f's `commits any act which he knows is prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different racial groups` AND f's `which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility`))

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 298A of the Penal Code 1871 (promoting enmity between different groups on grounds of race and doing acts prejudicial to maintenance of harmony)
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 298A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND `promotes enmity between racial groups` f

@export Frame a charge under section 298A of the Penal Code 1871 (promoting enmity between different groups on grounds of race and doing acts prejudicial to maintenance of harmony), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Racial Feelings Facts` @desc What the accused said, did or showed, and with what intention or knowledge, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 298A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "298A" "promoting enmity between different groups on grounds of race and doing acts prejudicial to maintenance of harmony"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 298A`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 298A` f)
        (CONCAT "did knowingly promote or attempt to promote, on grounds of race, disharmony or feelings of enmity, hatred or ill will between different racial groups, or commit an act which you knew was prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different racial groups and which disturbed or was likely to disturb the public tranquility", (`to wit` (f's `what was done`)))
        (concat (LIST
                (`missing unless` ((f's `by words, signs, visible representations or otherwise, knowingly promotes or attempts to promote, on grounds of race, disharmony or feelings of enmity, hatred or ill will between different racial groups` OR (f's `commits any act which he knows is prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different racial groups` AND f's `which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility`))) "(a) knowingly promotes or attempts to promote racial disharmony, enmity, hatred or ill will, or (b) commits an act he knows is prejudicial to racial harmony which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility"),
                (`missing unless` (`promotes enmity between racial groups` f) "the elements of section 298A taken together")))
